task_spec.prompt:
Refactor internal/csvutil/csvutil.go: introduce a CSVReader struct and move parsing/filtering logic to method receivers while keeping free functions as thin wrappers.

Add:
  type CSVReader struct {
      Separator rune  // field separator; defaults to ','
      LazyQuotes bool  // if true, relaxes CSV quoting rules
  }

  func NewCSVReader() *CSVReader  // returns CSVReader with Separator=',', LazyQuotes=false
  func (r *CSVReader) Parse(path string) ([][]string, error)   // reads file, returns all records
  func (r *CSVReader) Count(path string) (int, error)          // returns data rows (excl. header)
  func (r *CSVReader) Filter(path string, pred func([]string) bool) ([][]string, error)

Keep existing free functions as thin delegating wrappers:
  func ParseCSV(path string) ([][]string, error)           { return NewCSVReader().Parse(path) }
  func CountRows(path string) (int, error)                 { return NewCSVReader().Count(path) }
  func FilterCSV(path string, pred func([]string) bool) ([][]string, error) { return NewCSVReader().Filter(path, pred) }
  func WriteCSV(path string, rows [][]string) error        // keep existing implementation unchanged

All 4 existing tests must pass without modification.
Run: go test ./...
